==Spanish==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|es|osp|lançar}}, from {{inh|es|LL.|lanceō|lanceāre}}, derived from {{der|es|la|lancea||spear}}, of {{der|es|xce|-}} origin. Compare {{cog|ca|llançar}}, {{cog|ast|llanzar}}, {{cog|fr|lancer}}, {{cog|it|lanciare}}, {{cog|oc|-}} and {{cog|pt|lançar}}, {{cog|en|launch}}. {{doublet|es|lancear}}, a later borrowing.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr|+<audio:LL-Q1321 (spa)-AdrianAbdulBaha-lanzar.wav;Audio (Colombia)>}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb}}

# to [[throw]]
#: {{syn|es|arrojar|tirar|aventar}}
#: {{ux|es|El bebé '''lanzó''' el juguete con todas sus fuerzas.|The baby '''threw''' the toy with all his strength.}}
# to [[launch]]
# {{lb|es|baseball}} to [[pitch]]
#: {{ux|es|No pude lidiar con el modo en que '''lanzaba''' ese tipo.|I couldn't deal with how that guy '''pitched'''.}}

